WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.452
LENGTH is useful because text problems are not always visually obvious.

00:00:04.452 --> 00:00:09.547
Boundary spaces and repeated internal spaces increase the character count.

00:00:09.547 --> 00:00:16.497
Comparing length before and after cleaning can help confirm that your transformation is doing what you expect.

00:00:16.497 --> 00:00:20.852
Think of LENGTH as a diagnostic function during data preparation.

00:00:20.852 --> 00:00:24.977
Text cleaning should separate normalization from interpretation.

00:00:24.977 --> 00:00:30.347
Trimming spaces or standardizing case is usually safe when the rule is documented;

00:00:30.347 --> 00:00:35.297
correcting a person's name or guessing an email address is a much stronger intervention.

00:00:35.297 --> 00:00:38.545
Preserve the original value when auditability matters.
